WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.433
Embedded security continues after the
first firmware build.

2
00:00:03.513 --> 00:00:07.067
Teams should define how firmware
authenticity and integrity are checked,

3
00:00:07.147 --> 00:00:10.081
how updates are delivered, how failed
updates are recovered,

4
00:00:10.161 --> 00:00:14.053
how rollback policy works, and how devices
report version and health in the field.

5
00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:17.687
Update behavior should be designed as a
lifecycle, not a single operation.

6
00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.644
The device may lose power, receive an
incompatible package,

7
00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:24.052
encounter a storage failure, or need to
recover to a known-good state.

8
00:00:24.132 --> 00:00:27.348
Defensive design documents the expected
behavior before, during,

9
00:00:27.428 --> 00:00:28.725
and after update attempts.

10
00:00:28.805 --> 00:00:32.867
Debug and maintenance interfaces should be
controlled according to product risk and

11
00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:33.906
operational needs.

12
00:00:33.986 --> 00:00:36.130
The goal is not to remove all
serviceability.

13
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.820
The goal is to ensure that debug access,
diagnostics, manufacturing modes,

14
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.680
and maintenance workflows match the threat
model and are not accidentally left

15
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:44.888
broader than intended.

16
00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.717
Build and release practices matter.

17
00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:50.576
Toolchains, dependencies, features,
generated code, linker configuration,

18
00:00:50.656 --> 00:00:53.985
firmware artifacts, symbols, signing
materials, version metadata,

19
00:00:54.065 --> 00:00:55.644
and release logs all need review.

20
00:00:55.724 --> 00:00:59.447
These items are part of the firmware's
trust story because they influence what

21
00:00:59.527 --> 00:01:00.317
actually ships.

22
00:01:00.397 --> 00:01:03.274
Production hardening should be documented
and repeatable.

23
00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:07.303
Engineering, manufacturing, and
field-support teams should not rely on memory or

24
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:11.162
informal steps to know which build
settings, debug policies, artifact checks,

25
00:01:11.242 --> 00:01:12.935
and release evidence are required.

26
00:01:13.015 --> 00:01:14.820
Repeatability is a security control.
